Lazy loading is enabled. `db.Tickets` matches 40 rows for this owner.

```csharp
var tickets = await db.Tickets
    .Where(t => t.OwnerId == ownerId)
    .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)
    .ToListAsync();

var summaries = new List<string>();
foreach (var ticket in tickets)
{
    summaries.Add($"{ticket.Subject}: {ticket.Comments.Count} comments");
}
```

How many SQL queries does this send, and which line is responsible for the ones after the first?

solution.code:
function untrackedReadCandidates(queries) {
  const candidates = queries.filter(q => q.writes === false && q.tracked === true);
  return candidates.map(q => q.id);
}

grading.starterCode:
function untrackedReadCandidates(queries) {
  // Which of these are read-only AND still tracked?
  return queries.map(q => q.id);
}
